@startuml
' bt-view-kind: context
' bt-view-id: security-governance:security-context
title Security Governance - Context
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

' bt-element-id: player
' bt-element-id: operator
' bt-element-id: security

actor "Player\nResponsibility: Authenticate and access owned sessions\nContract: Least-privilege user session\n[[../../../../frontend/app/auth.py source]]" as player
actor "Operator\nResponsibility: Manage providers, policies and security settings\nContract: Privileged authenticated action\n[[../../../../administration-tool/app.py source]]" as operator
rectangle "Security Governance\nResponsibility: Authorize, protect and audit sensitive operations\nContract: Backend-owned policy boundary\n[[../../../../backend/app/services/governance/security_governance_service.py source]]" as security

operator ..> security : "requests privileged mutation\ncontract: role and CSRF checks"
player ..> security : "authenticates\ncontract: user session"

legend bottom
Viewpoint: context
Concern: Player and operator trust relationships with backend security authority
Elements expose responsibility, contract and source anchor.
Edges name the interaction or dependency contract.
endlegend
@enduml
